  "articleBody": "Choosing the right non-slip kitchen flooring can be a bit of a balancing act, right? You want something safe, but also easy to clean and comfortable. When you're shopping around, think about measured slip resistance—it's more reliable than just assuming a textured surface is safe. You'll also want to consider how easy it is to clean, because spills are just part of kitchen life, and you don't want cleaning products to reduce traction. Durability is a big one too; kitchen floors take a beating. Moisture tolerance is another key factor since wet zones around sinks and dishwashers are prime spots for slips. And hey, if you spend a lot of time cooking, comfort for long standing periods matters! For homes where accessibility is a priority, make sure the surface is stable for walkers or wheelchairs and that any transitions between different flooring types are low and smooth. Sometimes, getting an expert opinion can really help you weigh all these factors and make the best choice for your home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}